```

<<~ ahu #/bearing>>
! Art Sigils — Procedure Grammar

The smallest portable form carries *its own* native TW5 procedure definition and one named-argument invocation. A native TW5 instance transcludes the call into concise prose; a model familiar with wikitext may also directly interpret its semantic structure. Neither path guarantees the same response across image models.

The art-house lexicons live in the semantic specification and **inside values**, not in one procedure per artistic term. Only independently meaningful structural scopes warrant extended procedures. The 1,024-character envelope applies to the Inscription's transmitted definition and call together, never to the Folio or file metadata.
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/inscription>>
!! Canonical Inscription procedure

In portable use copy the next single line, followed by a blank line and one invocation. For image-facing calls use the new-style named parameter form (an equals sign followed by a backtick-delimited literal) instead of double-quoted argument values. Procedure declarations use the colon plus double-quoted default convention (`worktype:"artwork"`, `treatment:"suit the read"`); image-facing calls use an equals sign and single-backtick-delimited values (`treatment=`...``). Do not transpose these two grammars.

```tiddlywiki
\procedure art-sigil(worktype:"artwork" subject read imagery:"follow subject and read" treatment:"suit the read" composition:"serve the read" relation:"where meaningful" depiction-scope:"follow worktype and imagery") <<worktype>>: <<subject>>. Read: <<read>>. Imagery: <<imagery>>. Treatment: <<treatment>>. Composition: <<composition>>. Relation: <<relation>>. Depiction scope: <<depiction-scope>>.
```

* The eight semantic dimensions: worktype, subject, read, imagery, treatment, composition, relation, depiction-scope. Procedure definitions use `name:"default"`; invocations use TW5 v5.4.0+ `name=`value``. A supplied invocation value overrides its default; an omitted value inherits it. Keep both syntaxes exact.
* `subject` and `read` carry no explicit default; the authoring convention strongly prefers both. Other fields offer neutral or delegating defaults. Blank/silent values remain possible but the compact transclusion may then emit an empty label; do not mistake a blank for a creative instruction.
* A declaration default such as `composition:"serve the read"` supplies literal words for TW5 to transclude; an AI or human interprets that artistic invitation. Quotes inside a backtick call value survive as characters inside the rendered text; they do not function as parameter delimiters. No assumption of dynamic evaluation or of guaranteed AI understanding follows.
* The declared defaults invite artistic freedom: omitted imagery follows subject and read, treatment suits the read, composition serves the read, relation arises only where meaningful, and scope follows worktype and imagery. Explicit values take precedence.
* The procedure's subject and read do not prescribe genre, palette, medium, figures or photographic style. Context may deepen the *reading*, never secretly transplant source metadata as image content.
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/folio-modules>>
!! First Folio modules — provisional, not a complete procedure taxonomy

A Folio may expand a nucleus parameter in ordinary art language without any additional module. Invoke a module only when separately scoped evidence, media or pictorial argument deserves its own repeatable clause. Do not let this first trio foreclose future operators or vocabularies.

```tiddlywiki
\procedure art-study(question form proposal status:"unresolved") Study: <<question>>. Work: <<form>>. Proposal: <<proposal>>. Status: <<status>>.
\procedure art-counterpoint(first second tension evidence:"visible in the images") Counterpoint: <<first>> meets <<second>>; <<tension>>. Evidence: <<evidence>>.
\procedure art-facture(scope support medium handling:"let the medium's behavior remain visible") Facture in <<scope>>: <<medium>> on <<support>>; <<handling>>.
```

''Study'' contributes an independently interpretable attempt at a design question. ''Counterpoint'' lets two works, forms, histories or hypotheses act on each other; a mere overlap does not establish disagreement. ''Facture'' gives one scope its own physical support and medium behavior rather than spreading identical texture across every surface.

The distinct worktype, subject, read, imagery, treatment, composition, relation and depiction-scope fields already handle most paintings, drawings, maps, portraits and illustrations. No study, counterpoint or facture call follows automatically from the existence of a Folio.
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/sample>>
!! Generic use outside Example Zero

```tiddlywiki
<<art-sigil worktype=`brush-and-ink illustration` subject=`an abandoned tidal station` read=`a quiet place suggesting recent hurried departure` composition=`low horizon, long still reflection` relation=`a single warm window questions the apparent emptiness`>>
<<art-study question=`How high did the water rise?` form=`graphite floodline study` proposal=`two alternate staining heights on the same masonry` status=`provisional`>>
<<art-counterpoint first=`distant calm water` second=`broken floating lanterns` tension=`the stillness carries evidence of recent violence` evidence=`opposed edges and reflections`>>
<<art-facture scope=`foreground study paper` support=`smooth Bristol` medium=`sepia ink with drybrush` handling=`limited feathering, decisive exposed highlights`>>
```

The source uses a changed subject, not one disguised inheritance of Olympos. Copy the generic procedures as native pragmas into a TW5 context with the calls available at transclusion time. `<<~ name ...>>` belongs to Lares house sigils, not a synonym for native `<<name ...>>` calls.
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/notation-contract>>
!! Declaration/call split — two distinct syntaxes

* **Declaration:** `\procedure art-sigil(worktype:"artwork" read ... )` declares defaults with a colon and double quotes. No backticks for defaults in this project. The same convention applies to the three optional Folio procedures.
* **Invocation:** a native TW5 v5.4.0+ call, such as `<<art-sigil subject=`an explorer's "lost" road` read=`the uncertain route invites care`>>`, supplies an equals-sign named argument and a backtick-delimited value.
* **Substitution caveat:** TW5's backtick values permit its substitution placeholders. Portable literal Inscription values should contain no unintentional `$(...)<!-- <<~ !DOCTYPE = lar:///ha.ka.ba/art-sigils/procedures >> -->
